.TH CHANGE-IP 8 "September 2026" "ChangeIP 3.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
change-ip \- make a provider-issued IPv4 the default outbound source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B change-ip
.br
.B change-ip
.RB [ status | doctor | rollback | update ]
.br
.B change-ip
.I NEW_IP[/PREFIX]
.RI [ INTERFACE ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds or reuses an IPv4 address and makes it the explicit source of the selected
default IPv4 route through Linux netlink. Existing addresses and IPv6 are kept.
Metric and routing table are preserved. Off-subnet and /32 gateways use a
link-scope host route and onlink.
.PP
Persistence is a generated systemd oneshot invoking ChangeIP after
network-online.target. It does not replace cloud-init, Netplan, NetworkManager,
systemd-networkd, or ifupdown configuration.
.PP
With no arguments on a TTY, ChangeIP starts an inline interactive CLI. It uses
temporary raw input and ANSI updates, without an alternate-screen UI framework.
Use the arrow keys or j/k to navigate, Enter to select, Escape to go back, and q
to quit from the main screen. The terminal mode and cursor are restored on exit
or interruption. English is the default UI language; the Language menu item
switches between English and Russian and stores the choice in
.IR /etc/change-ip/language .
Set NO_COLOR to disable colors. Explicit commands remain plain text and are
suitable for non-interactive SSH use and pipelines.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status [INTERFACE]
Show addresses, outbound source, gateway, default route, desired boot state,
and systemd unit state.
.TP
.B doctor [INTERFACE]
Diagnose drift, missing/failed configuration, and unfinished transactions.
.TP
.B rollback [BACKUP_DIR]
Restore a versioned JSON backup. Without a directory, show a TTY menu.
.TP
.B update
Download the latest GitHub Release for the current architecture, verify its
SHA-256 checksum, and atomically install it. Requires root and does not change
network state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --gateway , " -g " GW
Set the IPv4 gateway.
.TP
.BR --interface , " -i " IFACE
Use an explicit validated interface.
.TP
.BR --prefix , " -p " N
Set prefix length for an address without /N.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Discover, validate, snapshot, and plan without changing state.
.TP
.B --runtime-only
Skip backup and persistence.
.TP
.BR --yes , " -y"
Skip confirmation.
.TP
.B --check-egress
Also check the route to 8.8.8.8 and an external IPv4 API. API failure is only a warning.
.TP
.BI --profile " FILE"
Read strict IP/PREFIX and optional gateway entries.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/change-ip-addresses.conf
.br
.I /etc/change-ip/language
.br
.I /usr/local/lib/change-ip/apply-IFACE.json
.br
.I /etc/systemd/system/change-ip-IFACE.service
.br
.I /root/change-ip-backup.*/manifest.json
.SH UPDATE
Run
.B sudo change-ip update
to install the latest checksum-verified GitHub Release directly. For initial
installation or recovery, run the updater from a local checkout with
.B sudo ./update.sh
or fetch it from the repository. The new ELF is validated and atomically
installed before pre-3.0 scripts and deprecated
.B change_ip
commands are removed. The only command name is
.BR change-ip .
.B /usr/local/sbin/change-ip
is a same-name compatibility symlink to the canonical
.B /usr/local/bin/change-ip
binary for existing systemd units.
.SH SAFETY
Mutations hold /run/change-ip.lock. SIGINT, SIGTERM, and SIGHUP cause rollback
when possible. Interactive apply uses systemd-run when available for SSH safety.
.SH SEE ALSO
systemd(1), systemd-run(1), ip-route(8)
